<title>USA: Arco to buy another stake in China refinery.</title>
<headline>Arco to buy another stake in China refinery.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Atlantic Richfield Co (ARCO) said on Thursday it bought 64 percent of a convertible bond offering by China's Zhenhai Refining and Chemical Company (ZRCC).</p>
<p>The seven-year bonds would convert to 353 million Hong Kong-traded &quot;H&quot; shares, which would leave ARCO with a 591 million &quot;H&quot; share ownership, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>The shares would give ARCO a 20 percent interest in ZRCC, China's third largest oil refiner.</p>
<p>ARCO bought a smaller share of ZRCC in 1994.</p>
<p>Proceeds from the offering will help fund an expansion of refining capacity, the company said.</p>
</text>
